          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"flaubert-madame-bovary-400a3aed5a88\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":1,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.93,\"analysis\":\"The highlighted “je t’aime” primarily avows the speaker’s loving state, which she immediately elaborates as dependence, jealousy, and intense admiration. The wider speech weakly suggests relational self-commitment through declarations of service and submission, but the core utterance does not clearly undertake an obligation. Its exclamatory, passionate delivery does not independently establish reflex-like expressive force.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The surrounding claims “Je suis ta servante et ta concubine” give limited support to a performative reading, though they more naturally characterize the avowed love than make “je t’aime” itself a commitment.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"A directly spoken declaration in narrated dialogue; the highlighted occurrence is the first “je t’aime,” introduced by “Oh! c’est que” and followed by a repeated declaration.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"The declaration belongs to an extended, highly emotional profession of dependence, jealousy, devotion, and idealization. Repetition, exclamations, and hyperbole intensify the avowal, while “reprenait-elle” presents it as continued discourse rather than an involuntary blurt. Whatever the sincerity or durability of these feelings, the utterance presents love as true and is adequately represented mainly by T.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Oh! c’est que je t’aime! reprenait-elle, je t’aime à ne pouvoir me passer de toi”\",\"supports\":\"The speaker directly and repeatedly avows love and describes it as an inability to do without the addressee, strongly supporting T.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“J’ai quelquefois des envies de te revoir où toutes les colères de l’amour me déchirent.”\",\"supports\":\"The speaker explicitly attributes longing and emotional torment to love, reinforcing the truth-conditional presentation of an affective state.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Je suis ta servante et ta concubine! Tu es mon roi, mon idole!”\",\"supports\":\"These declarations frame the love as relational devotion and self-subordination, supplying weak support for commitment-like force but not clearly making the highlighted words an undertaking.\",\"confidence\":0.9},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The narration uses “reprenait-elle” before a sustained sequence of articulated claims, questions, and comparisons.\",\"supports\":\"The speech is presented as resumed and elaborated discourse; emotional punctuation alone does not provide positive evidence that “je t’aime” is a reflex-like verbal discharge, supporting E=0.\",\"confidence\":0.89}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T captures the central avowal, with slight P support for the relational submission developed around it. Emotional intensity is contextual and does not require E or O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
